<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zionism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zionist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zionism is the nationalist movement that emerged in the late nineteenth century to establish a Jewish national homeland in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>. Its political form was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodor-herzl">Theodor Herzl</a>, whose writings and organisation of the first Zionist Congress in 1897 gave it international shape. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> list Zionist political theory among the intellectual products of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fin-de-siecle">fin-de-siècle</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…century was one of the intellectual capitals of the Western world, producing the foundations of psychoanalysis (Freud), political <b>Zionism</b> (Herzl), the art of the Secession and Expressionism (Klimt, Schiele, Kokoschka), the Second Viennese School of music (Schoenberg, Berg, Webern), and the Austrian school of economics (Menger), while nurturing…</blockquote><a href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 19th and early 20th centuries millions of Jews emigrated from Eastern Europe to the Americas, especially the United States, and <b>Zionism</b> called for a Jewish national home in the land of Israel.</blockquote><a href="/religion/judaism">Judaism · Spread</a></li><li><blockquote>…members in the United Nations General Assembly, with Arab countries and the support of the Soviet bloc, pushed through Resolution 3379, a non-binding measure that equated <b>Zionism</b> with South Africa’s apartheid as a form of racial discrimination; the same year the movement created the Non-Aligned News Agencies Pool.</blockquote><a href="/movement/non-aligned-movement">Non-Aligned Movement · Course of Events</a></li><li><blockquote>Jewish nationalism, <b>Zionism</b>, answered antisemitism and pogroms with settlement in Palestine from 1882.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/nationalism">Nationalism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>Only under Gamal Abdel Nasser did Arab nationalism, with Arab socialism, become Egypt’s state policy, usually set against <b>Zionism</b> in neighbouring Israel.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/pan-arabism">Pan-Arabism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>Many communities, especially those of religious <b>Zionism</b>, recite it on Israeli Independence Day, as the Chief Rabbinate of Israel instructs, and some on Jerusalem Day.</blockquote><a href="/songs/hallel">Hallel</a></li></ul></section>
